  "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1-4\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3+2\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{1-4\\text{i}} \\\\ (-3+2\\text{i})(1-4\\text{i}) & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ -3+12\\text{i}+2\\text{i}-8{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ -3+8+14\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 5+14\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n5=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=5$ and $q=14.$",
